.\" Manual page for git-reviewer. git opens this for `git reviewer --help`,
.\" because it reads --help on any subcommand as a request for its man page.
.TH GIT-REVIEWER 1 "2026-09-25" "git-reviewer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-reviewer, reviewer \- review local git changes in your browser, and hand the review to a coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git reviewer
.RI [ repository ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-open ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-untracked ]
.br
.B git reviewer export
.RI [ repository ]
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR json | prompt ]
.RB [ \-\-file
.IR path ]
.br
.B git reviewer connect
.RI [ repository ]
.RB [ \-\-session
.IR id ]
.RB [ \-\-fork ]
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.br
.B git reviewer reply
.I key text
.RB [ \-\-repo
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-as
.IR name ]
.br
.B git reviewer watch
.RI [ repository ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the uncommitted changes of a git repository, or its last commit on a
clean tree, as a pull-request style review in your browser: inline comments
on any line, threaded follow-ups, and comparisons between branches, tags and
commits \(em reviewed together, one at a time, or as a run.
.PP
With something reading its output, it writes the finished review there the
moment you submit it, and exits:
.PP
.RS
.B git reviewer | claude \-p "Apply this review."
.RE
.PP
On a terminal it says where the review was saved and keeps serving until
the tab is closed.
.PP
The package is installed as
.BR git\-reviewer ,
which git runs as
.BR "git reviewer" .
.B reviewer
is the same program under a shorter name.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B export
Print the saved review of a repository to stdout, as JSON or as a prompt for
a coding agent.
.TP
.B connect
Resume the Claude Code session that worked in the repository, with reviewer
attached as a channel: every comment written in the review is sent to the
session as it is written, and the session answers in the thread.
.B \-\-list
shows the sessions;
.B \-\-session
picks one by id or id prefix;
.B \-\-fork
resumes a copy. Claude Code asks once, at startup, to confirm the channel.
.TP
.B reply
Post a reply in a comment thread, as an agent. Inside Claude Code it is
signed
.BR claude ,
elsewhere
.B agent
unless
.B \-\-as
names who it is from. Exits 1 if no comment has that key.
.TP
.B watch
Print each comment waiting for an answer, then each new comment or reply
from the reviewer, as one JSON line, until interrupted.
.TP
.B channel
The MCP server
.B connect
asks Claude Code to run, speaking JSON-RPC over stdio. Not run by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIn\fR"
Port to listen on. The default is 4500; if it is taken, a free one is used.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Print the address instead of opening a browser.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-intro
Open the review without the first-run help. The ? button still opens it.
The page is told with
.B intro=0
in the URL.
.TP
.B \-\-staged
Review only staged changes, comparing HEAD with the index. Unstaged edits are
excluded, and an empty index comparison does not fall back to the last commit.
.TP
.BI \-\-range " base" ... head
Open a comparison instead of the uncommitted changes: what
.I head
changed since it left
.IR base ,
as its pull request shows it, with the pickers set as if
.B Compare branches
had chosen it.
.B ..
means the same as
.B ...
here, and an empty end is HEAD, so
.B \-\-range origin/main...
compares the current branch with origin/main.
.TP
.BI \-\-base " ref"
The same as
.BI \-\-range " ref" ...HEAD:
the whole branch.
.TP
.BI \-\-commit " rev"
Open one commit, as clicking it in the commit list does.
.TP
.B \-\-last\-commit
Open HEAD on its own.
.PP
.RS
These four are exclusive with each other and with
.BR \-\-staged .
A ref that does not name a commit fails in the terminal before anything is
served. The URL each one opens can be shared.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-no\-untracked
Exclude untracked files from working directory reviews. Tracked changes remain
reviewable. This option is only valid when serving a review.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIjson\fR|\fIprompt\fR"
Export format. The default is json.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " path"
Export only the comments on one repository-relative file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage. Under git, use
.BR \-h :
git takes
.B \-\-help
to mean this page.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git reviewer
Review the repository you are standing in.
.TP
.B git reviewer | claude \-p """Apply this review."""
Review it, then hand it straight to an agent.
.TP
.B git reviewer export . \-\-format prompt | claude \-p """Apply this review."""
Hand over a review written earlier.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/dheerajjha/reviewer
